    "event": {
      "address": "Vernon Square, Penton Rise, London WC1X 9EW",
      "category": "talk",
      "dedupe_key": "untold-tales-women-pioneers-in-british-irish-architectural-history|2026-11-13|courtauld-vernon-square",
      "description": "There have been a growing number of studies of female architects over the past twenty years but almost no accounts of female architectural historians. One exception is Dana Arnold’s edited collection Women and Architectural History: The Monstrous Regiment Then and Now (2025) which involved women operating from the 1970s onwards. This symposium looks back further to the earliest generations involved in the writing and promotion of architectural history in a wide range of spheres. We are interested in women who were involved in the subject as academics, curators, journalists, photographers, writers and in the conservation and heritage spheres from the nineteenth century onwards. Organised by Dr Kyle Leyden, Lecturer in Early Modern Architecture and Visual Culture, the Courtauld; Dr Manolo Guerci, Reader in Architecture, University of Kent and Prof. Elizabeth McKellar, President, SAHGB. Supported by the Paul Mellon Centre for Studies in British Art and The Institute of Historic Building Conservation.",
      "ends_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z",
      "image_url": null,
      "lat": 51.5298,
      "lng": -0.1164,
      "price": {
