s=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">fraught </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">topics of </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">descent and inheritance through an examination of Victorian paintings of mothers and their children, with particular attention paid to depictions of </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">infants</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">who</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\"> look different from their mothers</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">. These complex representations of matrilineal descent are revealing of the</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\"> challenges involved in </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">identifying</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\"> and portraying</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\"> racial lineages</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">, and undermine systems of racial classification based on skin, </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">hair</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\"> and eye colour</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">A case in point is </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">Dante Gabriel Rossetti’s </span></span><em><span class=\"TextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\" data-contrast=\"none\" lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">The Beloved</span></span></em><span class=\"TextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\" data-contrast=\"none\" lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">(1865-6), a highly racialised illustration of the </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">Hebrew Bible’s </span></span><span class=\"TextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\" data-contrast=\"none\" lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">Song of Songs</span></span><span class=\"TextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\" data-contrast=\"none\" lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\"> and Psalm 45</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">In addition to the fair-skinned bride and racially diverse bridesmaids, Rossetti included in </span></span><em><span class=\"TextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\" data-contrast=\"none\" lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">The Beloved</span></span></em><span class=\"TextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\" data-contrast=\"none\" lang=\"EN-GB\" xml:lang=\"EN-GB\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\"> a depiction of a Black child. By </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">speculating</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\"> on the relationship of the child to other figures inside and outside the frame, Hammerschlag finds </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW73662580 BCX4\">traces of the trauma of forced removal of ‘mixed-race’ children from their mothers, which was practiced under both American slavery and British colonialism.</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW73662580 BCX4\" data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:360,&quot;469777462&quot;:[2785],&quot;469777927&quot;:[0],&quot;469777928&quot;:[1]}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong>This event is organised by <a href=\"https://courtauld.ac.uk/people/steve-edwards/\">Professor Steve Edwards,</a> Manton Professor of British Art and Director of the Manton Centre for British Art, The Courtauld.</strong></p>",
